# Knowledge against a reading (tasks.org, aida-referents-anaphora-knowledge;
# after the author's tests/anaphora/multiple_dynamic.fspy). Alone,
# he_bites_him resolves both pronouns to the donkey, the latest antecedent.
# no_self_biting presumes, of anybody, that they do not bite themselves:
# its generic statement covers the readings bites !donkey !donkey and
# bites !farmer !farmer, no node of the document. Two presumptions on one
# statement: both sides UNDEC (an onus conflict, warned), and the second
# pronoun falls back to the farmer. The argued spelling is
# self_biting_argued.fspy.
lk.
pipeline unfolded.
declare iota : type.
declare farmer, donkey : iota -> bool.
declare has, bites : iota -> iota -> bool.
argument a_farmer_has_a_donkey : [!farmer:iota,!donkey:iota] exists x:iota, exists y:iota, farmer [x] - ~donkey [y] - ~has [x] [y].
elim [!farmer].
elim [!donkey].
by default.
dixi.
argument he_bites_him : [?c:iota,?d:iota] exists x:iota, exists y:iota, bites [x] [y].
elim [?c].
elim [?d].
by default.
dixi.
counterargument no_self_biting : [!z:iota] bites [!z] [!z].
by default.
dixi.
